;
SDZ - SUPER DIRECTORY

CALLER. Subject to current caller access policy.

A - Super Directory

:A
SUPER DIRECTORY

    SDZ
    SDZ HELP:
    SDZ P0:*.LBR

SDZ and DIR are the same supplied Super Directory (SD 1.37) utility.
Both names accept the same public directory-listing syntax.

Use a DU or named directory to examine a particular area. Wildcards
can narrow the listing to filenames or extensions of interest. The
listing gives allocated file sizes, matched totals and drive free space.

Some original SD options are reserved to the private sysop, including
printer or disk output, disk reset and privileged attribute listings.
A caller cannot use SDZ to bypass directory permissions.

See HELP DIR for more examples and HELP CPM for DU conventions.
